// Q-1032 Svelte's `on:click={...}` gets "takes only text written here, as the browser runs it as code", which does not say to write `onclick`
// mode: check
// open-when: `on:click` in <button> takes only text written here, as the browser runs it as code
// fixed-when: /:11: error[^\n]*`onclick/
// From FEEDBACK72.md §Q-1032 (found on 238dac2, 0.8.6; open on 77ffcd0, 0.8.9). Refused,
// rightly; the message should name the spelling to use, as `@mouseEnter`'s does.

// Svelte's spelling of an event.
component Pot() {
    state n = 0
    <button on:click={() => { n += 1 }}>{n}</button>
}
route GET / = <html><body><Pot/></body></html>
